<?xml version="1.0" ?>
<sdf version="1.9">
  <world name="demo_area_2m5">
    <!--
      demo_area_2m5: the real demo environment, empty, created 2026-08-21.

      A 2.50 x 2.50 m area centred on the origin - 1.25 m in every direction
      "under the drone" (user decision 2026-08-21). It is the twin of the
      geofence set the same day in gripperx_external/config/octopus_link_twin.yaml
      (geofence.{min,max}_{x,y}_m = -+1.25), so what the gateway will accept and
      what the operator sees on the ground are the same rectangle.

      THE BOUNDARY IS VISUAL ONLY - NO COLLISION, ON PURPOSE.
      Real walls at -+1.25 would make this world useless for the thing it is for.
      Measured against the stack as configured (gripperx_planning/config/nav2.yaml):
        inflation_radius 0.50, cost_scaling_factor 7.0, inscribed radius 0.230,
        max_goal_cost 200 (gateway).
      Inflation cost is 252*exp(-7.0*(d - 0.230)) outside the inscribed circle, so
      against a solid wall:
        d < 0.230 m   LETHAL
        d ~ 0.25 m    cost ~219  -> above max_goal_cost, goal REFUSED
        d ~ 0.30 m    cost ~154  -> accepted
      i.e. the outer ~0.26 m ring of the box would be refused on COST while the
      geofence says it is inside. Two different mechanisms rejecting the same
      poses for different reasons is exactly the confusion this world exists to
      avoid: here the geofence is the ONLY boundary, and a refusal means what it
      says.

      WHY THERE IS AN OUTER ENCLOSURE AT -+4.0 m, IN AN "EMPTY" WORLD.
      A world with NOTHING solid in it does not work with this stack, and the
      failure is silent. Gazebo's LiDAR returns `inf` where nothing is hit;
      nav2's obstacle layer has `inf_is_valid` unset, i.e. FALSE, so those
      readings are DISCARDED instead of clearing the ray. The local costmap then
      stays NO_INFORMATION, and with `track_unknown_space: true` (nav2.yaml,
      deliberate) dwb_critics ObstacleFootprintCritic rejects every forward
      trajectory whose footprint crosses unknown ground - "Trajectory Hits
      Unknown Region". The robot would simply not move, for a reason that looks
      nothing like its cause.
      The enclosure gives the scan real returns, so the interior is raytraced
      FREE and SLAM has features to hold on to. It sits 2.75 m outside the
      geofence and inflation reaches only 0.50 m inward from it (to -+3.50 m), so
      it CANNOT touch the -+1.25 m box. The play area is empty where emptiness
      is the point.

      WHAT IT STILL DOES NOT TEST, STATED RATHER THAN HIDDEN: there is no
      obstacle inside the box, so nothing here exercises avoidance, and an
      unobstructed run is NOT evidence that it works. This world tests the
      Octopus link, the geofence, dispatch and arming. Obstacle handling belongs
      in testworld_simple.

      Origin convention: the world origin is the datum, i.e. the point under the
      drone. Spawn the robot at (0, 0) with spawn_yaw:=0.0 so that map, odom and
      world axes coincide and a target at map (x, y) is at world (x, y) with no
      rotation to reason about.
    -->
    <gravity>0 0 -9.81</gravity>
    <physics name="1ms" type="ignored">
      <!-- 0.001 -> 0.010 on 2026-08-24 (user decision), i.e. 100 Hz physics.
           MEASURED headless with the real model in testworld_v1, startup cost
           subtracted, 2 runs each: the cost per step is flat at ~1.0 ms
           regardless of step size, so the load scales linearly with the step
           COUNT. Max achievable real-time factor:
               0.001 -> 0.98-1.03x     0.002 -> 2.07-2.21x
               0.004 -> 3.77-4.01x     0.010 -> 9.97-11.59x
           At 0.001 the physics had NO headroom at all -- 1.0x headless, with no
           rendering, no gz_ros2_control, no bridge, no Nav2, no RViz. That is
           why the sim felt slow: real_time_factor 1.0 throttles the server to
           real time, and it was sitting exactly on that limit.

           WHY THIS IS AFFORDABLE HERE, and it is a statement about THIS model:
           a fine step buys fidelity only where there is stiff, tuned contact
           dynamics to resolve. There is none. Total simulated mass is 3.72 kg
           (arm_stowed_link weighs 1 GRAM, imu_link likewise, and chassis_link's
           2.27 kg is bare CAD shell -- no battery, Pi, motors or electronics);
           the real mass is not documented anywhere (internal REQUIREMENTS S25/HWR-32,
           "No CG/weight budget"). There is not one friction or contact
           parameter in the whole workspace -- no mu, mu2, slip, kp/kd, no
           <surface> -- so every tyre is Gazebo default on a smooth cylinder.
           Integrating placeholder numbers ten times more finely buys nothing.

           STABILITY, measured: dropped from 0.20 m onto the ground plane, the
           model settles 0.074 mm lower than at 0.001, with 0.33 mm of residual
           jitter and no tilt. Sub-millimetre against a 70 mm wheel radius.

           WHAT THIS DOES COST -- control-period jitter, see the note in
           gripperx_control/config/ros2_controllers.yaml (update_rate: 30).
           100 Hz does not divide by 30. ros2_control can only fire on a physics
           tick, so the 33.3 ms period becomes an alternating 30/40 ms one
           (-10 %/+20 %); at 0.001 the same quantisation was +-1.5 %. The period
           handed to the controllers is the true elapsed one, so odometry
           integration stays correct -- but any fixed-gain filter or rate limiter
           tuned at a steady 30 Hz now sees a varying period.
           1/120 s (0.008333) would divide 30 Hz exactly, giving ~8.3x instead
           of ~10x for zero jitter, if that trade is ever worth making. -->
      <max_step_size>0.010</max_step_size>
      <real_time_factor>1.0</real_time_factor>
    </physics>

    <plugin
      filename="gz-sim-physics-system"
      name="gz::sim::systems::Physics" />
    <plugin
      filename="gz-sim-user-commands-system"
      name="gz::sim::systems::UserCommands" />
    <plugin
      filename="gz-sim-scene-broadcaster-system"
      name="gz::sim::systems::SceneBroadcaster" />
    <plugin
      filename="gz-sim-contact-system"
      name="gz::sim::systems::Contact" />
    <plugin
      filename="gz-sim-imu-system"
      name="gz::sim::systems::Imu" />
    <plugin
      filename="gz-sim-sensors-system"
      name="gz::sim::systems::Sensors">
      <render_engine>ogre2</render_engine>
    </plugin>

    <light name="sun" type="directional">
      <!-- Shadows off 2026-08-24. A shadow map is a second full render pass over
           the scene per light, and on the development laptop's Intel UHD 620 that
           is paid for every GUI frame and every sensor frame. Nothing in this
           project reads shadows: the LiDAR is a gpu_lidar (range only, unlit) and
           no node subscribes to the camera. Purely cosmetic cost, so it is off by
           default. Set back to true if a scenario ever needs a lit image. -->
      <cast_shadows>false</cast_shadows>
      <pose>0 0 10 0 0 0</pose>
      <diffuse>0.8 0.8 0.8 1</diffuse>
      <specular>0.2 0.2 0.2 1</specular>
      <attenuation>
        <range>1000</range>
        <constant>0.9</constant>
        <linear>0.01</linear>
        <quadratic>0.001</quadratic>
      </attenuation>
      <direction>-0.5 0.1 -0.9</direction>
    </light>

    <model name="ground_plane">
      <static>true</static>
      <link name="link">
        <collision name="collision">
          <geometry>
            <plane><normal>0 0 1</normal><size>100 100</size></plane>
          </geometry>
        </collision>
        <visual name="visual">
          <geometry>
            <plane><normal>0 0 1</normal><size>100 100</size></plane>
          </geometry>
          <material>
            <ambient>0.8 0.8 0.8 1</ambient>
            <diffuse>0.8 0.8 0.8 1</diffuse>
          </material>
        </visual>
      </link>
    </model>

    <!--
      Outer enclosure at -+4.0 m. Present so the LiDAR has returns (see the
      header note); far enough that its inflation never reaches the play area.
    -->
    <model name="enclosure_north">
      <static>true</static>
      <pose>0 4 1.0 0 0 0</pose>
      <link name="link">
        <collision name="collision"><geometry><box><size>8.2 0.2 2.0</size></box></geometry></collision>
        <visual name="visual"><geometry><box><size>8.2 0.2 2.0</size></box></geometry></visual>
      </link>
    </model>
    <model name="enclosure_south">
      <static>true</static>
      <pose>0 -4 1.0 0 0 0</pose>
      <link name="link">
        <collision name="collision"><geometry><box><size>8.2 0.2 2.0</size></box></geometry></collision>
        <visual name="visual"><geometry><box><size>8.2 0.2 2.0</size></box></geometry></visual>
      </link>
    </model>
    <model name="enclosure_east">
      <static>true</static>
      <pose>4 0 1.0 0 0 0</pose>
      <link name="link">
        <collision name="collision"><geometry><box><size>0.2 8.2 2.0</size></box></geometry></collision>
        <visual name="visual"><geometry><box><size>0.2 8.2 2.0</size></box></geometry></visual>
      </link>
    </model>
    <model name="enclosure_west">
      <static>true</static>
      <pose>-4 0 1.0 0 0 0</pose>
      <link name="link">
        <collision name="collision"><geometry><box><size>0.2 8.2 2.0</size></box></geometry></collision>
        <visual name="visual"><geometry><box><size>0.2 8.2 2.0</size></box></geometry></visual>
      </link>
    </model>

    <!--
      The -+1.25 m boundary. Four flat strips lying on the ground, 40 mm wide,
      1 mm proud, NO <collision> element anywhere in this model - the LiDAR and
      the costmap cannot see it and it can never inflate.
    -->
    <model name="geofence_marker">
      <static>true</static>
      <link name="link">
        <visual name="edge_north">
          <pose>0 1.25 0.0005 0 0 0</pose>
          <geometry><box><size>2.54 0.04 0.001</size></box></geometry>
          <material>
            <ambient>0.9 0.55 0.1 1</ambient>
            <diffuse>0.9 0.55 0.1 1</diffuse>
          </material>
        </visual>
        <visual name="edge_south">
          <pose>0 -1.25 0.0005 0 0 0</pose>
          <geometry><box><size>2.54 0.04 0.001</size></box></geometry>
          <material>
            <ambient>0.9 0.55 0.1 1</ambient>
            <diffuse>0.9 0.55 0.1 1</diffuse>
          </material>
        </visual>
        <visual name="edge_east">
          <pose>1.25 0 0.0005 0 0 0</pose>
          <geometry><box><size>0.04 2.54 0.001</size></box></geometry>
          <material>
            <ambient>0.9 0.55 0.1 1</ambient>
            <diffuse>0.9 0.55 0.1 1</diffuse>
          </material>
        </visual>
        <visual name="edge_west">
          <pose>-1.25 0 0.0005 0 0 0</pose>
          <geometry><box><size>0.04 2.54 0.001</size></box></geometry>
          <material>
            <ambient>0.9 0.55 0.1 1</ambient>
            <diffuse>0.9 0.55 0.1 1</diffuse>
          </material>
        </visual>
        <!-- The datum: map (0,0), the point under the drone. -->
        <visual name="datum_x">
          <pose>0 0 0.0005 0 0 0</pose>
          <geometry><box><size>0.30 0.02 0.001</size></box></geometry>
          <material>
            <ambient>0.1 0.4 0.9 1</ambient>
            <diffuse>0.1 0.4 0.9 1</diffuse>
          </material>
        </visual>
        <visual name="datum_y">
          <pose>0 0 0.0005 0 0 0</pose>
          <geometry><box><size>0.02 0.30 0.001</size></box></geometry>
          <material>
            <ambient>0.1 0.4 0.9 1</ambient>
            <diffuse>0.1 0.4 0.9 1</diffuse>
          </material>
        </visual>
      </link>
    </model>
  </world>
</sdf>
